---
title: Code
description: Syntax highlighting with the system's own tokeniser and colour theme, plus a copy button. About 3 KB, no library — and it upgrades exactly the markup Ghost's code card emits.
eyebrow: Component
source: src/js/im-code.js · src/components/code.css · src/foundation/tokens/code.css
---
<h2>Use it</h2>
<p>Load <code>im-code.js</code>. Every <code>&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code class="language-…"&gt;</code> on the page gets a header with the language and a copy button, and its tokens coloured. In Ghost that is every code card — authors pick the language in the editor and nothing else is needed.</p>
{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
<script src="{{asset "im-code.js"}}" defer></script>
{{{{/code}}}}
<p>Without the script a <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> still looks right; it just has no colours and no button. Content added later: <code>imCode.highlight(element)</code>.</p>

<h2>Languages</h2>
{{{{code "js"}}}}
// JavaScript · TypeScript · JSX
import { readTokens } from './lib/tokens.mjs';

export async function build({ quiet = false } = {}) {
	const started = Date.now();
	const tokens = readTokens();          /* two tiers */
	if (!quiet) console.log(`built ${tokens.count} tokens in ${Date.now() - started}ms`);
	return tokens.count > 0 ? true : null;
}
{{{{/code}}}}
